{
  "duration": 64.579,
  "phrases": [
    {
      "start": 0.099,
      "end": 1.139,
      "text": "So welcome back again."
    },
    {
      "start": 1.759,
      "end": 3.24,
      "text": "It's time to solve one more problem."
    },
    {
      "start": 3.699,
      "end": 5.319,
      "text": "Now in this problem, we are given that"
    },
    {
      "start": 5.799,
      "end": 6.46,
      "text": "tan theta"
    },
    {
      "start": 7.019,
      "end": 9.099,
      "text": "is equal to seven by twenty-four,"
    },
    {
      "start": 9.719,
      "end": 11.639,
      "text": "and theta is an acute angle."
    },
    {
      "start": 12.239,
      "end": 14.399,
      "text": "The problem is asking us to find sec theta."
    },
    {
      "start": 15.039,
      "end": 18.079,
      "text": "So tan theta is equal to perpendicular upon base."
    },
    {
      "start": 18.539,
      "end": 19.439,
      "text": "Comparing this with"
    },
    {
      "start": 19.84,
      "end": 20.479,
      "text": "tan theta"
    },
    {
      "start": 20.979,
      "end": 26.879,
      "text": "equals seven by twenty-four, we get perpendicular equals seven and base equals twenty-four."
    },
    {
      "start": 27.34,
      "end": 27.619,
      "text": "Done."
    },
    {
      "start": 28.159,
      "end": 31.179,
      "text": "We now know two sides of the right triangle. We just need the third side."
    },
    {
      "start": 31.479,
      "end": 32.739,
      "text": "To find the hypotenuse,"
    },
    {
      "start": 33.079,
      "end": 36.779,
      "text": "we will use the Pythagoras theorem. Hypotenuse equals square root of"
    },
    {
      "start": 37.239,
      "end": 40.219,
      "text": "perpendicular square plus base square."
    },
    {
      "start": 40.619,
      "end": 41.839,
      "text": "Substitute the values."
    },
    {
      "start": 42.219,
      "end": 46.279,
      "text": "Hypotenuse equals square root of seven square plus twenty-four square."
    },
    {
      "start": 46.819,
      "end": 50.739,
      "text": "After simplifying, hypotenuse equals square root of six hundred twenty-five,"
    },
    {
      "start": 51.139,
      "end": 52.52,
      "text": "which is equal to twenty-five."
    },
    {
      "start": 53.02,
      "end": 56.319,
      "text": "Now we know that sec theta equals hypotenuse upon base."
    },
    {
      "start": 56.799,
      "end": 57.959,
      "text": "Substitute the values."
    },
    {
      "start": 58.379,
      "end": 60.759,
      "text": "Sec theta equals twenty-five by twenty-four."
    },
    {
      "start": 61.479,
      "end": 61.859,
      "text": "Hence,"
    },
    {
      "start": 62.239,
      "end": 64.579,
      "text": "the correct option is option C."
    }
  ],
